This product includes software from the Termux project
(https://github.com/termux/termux-app), commit 8629e632fcb95da272221be327db653fb24befe9:
the terminal-emulator and terminal-view libraries, which are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 and derive from Jack Palevich's Android Terminal
Emulator (https://github.com/jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator).

They are vendored in terminal/ with these modifications:
- com.termux.terminal.TerminalSession no longer spawns a local process through
  JNI; it is fed by a remote byte stream (an SSH PTY channel) via a Transport
  interface. JNI.java and the native code were removed.
- TerminalSessionClient#setTerminalShellPid was removed (there is no local PID).
- OSC 52 (remote clipboard writes) goes to a new TerminalSessionClient#onRemoteClipboardCopy,
  separate from local "Copy" of a selection (TerminalSession#copyLocalSelection).
- terminal-view's strings were translated to Spanish.

It also uses, as dependencies (not vendored): sshj (Apache 2.0),
Bouncy Castle (MIT-style Bouncy Castle License), AndroidX / Jetpack Compose and
kotlinx libraries (Apache 2.0).

